# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk F (Frostbitten Fingers to Hunger of Leng). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Frostbitten Fingers": ["You fire a ray of intense cold at a creature. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, one of the target's hands goes numb.",
 "You fire a ray of intense cold at a creature. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, one of the target's hands goes numb. When the spell lands, the target makes a Dexterity save to keep hold of anything in that hand, and it must repeat the save each time it tries to use, wield or pick up an item with that hand. The target also has disadvantage on Dexterity and Strength checks that need both hands. After every 10 minutes under the spell, the target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 1d6 cold damage and loses a finger of the affected hand, starting with the pinkie."],
"Frozen Razors": ['Blades of razor-sharp ice burst from the ground or another surface and fill a 20-foot cube centered on a point you can see within range.',
 'Blades of razor-sharp ice burst from the ground or another surface and fill a 20-foot cube centered on a point you can see within range. The area is lightly obscured and is difficult terrain for the duration. A creature that moves more than 5 feet into or within the area on a turn makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 2d6 slashing damage and 3d6 cold damage, or half as much on a success. A creature that takes cold damage from this spell has its speed halved until the start of its next turn.'],
"Furious Hooves": ["You touch a creature and fill its feet or hooves with power and speed. The target's walking speed increases by 30 feet or doubles, whichever adds less.",
 "You touch a creature and fill its feet or hooves with power and speed. The target's walking speed increases by 30 feet or doubles, whichever adds less. It also gains two hoof attacks in addition to its normal attacks. Each hoof deals bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + its Strength modifier, or 1d8 + its Strength modifier if the target is Large. While the spell lasts, the target automatically deals this bludgeoning damage to a creature it successfully shoves."],
"Fusillade of Ice": ['You loose a spray of razor-sharp ice shards. Each creature in a 30-foot cone makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 4d6 cold damage and 3d6 piercing damage, or half as much on a success.',
 'You loose a spray of razor-sharp ice shards. Each creature in a 30-foot cone makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 4d6 cold damage and 3d6 piercing damage, or half as much on a success.'],
"Gear Barrage": ['A burst of magically driven gears sprays out in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a Dexterity save and takes 3d8 slashing damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.',
 'A burst of magically driven gears sprays out in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a Dexterity save and takes 3d8 slashing damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. Constructs have disadvantage on the save.'],
"Gear Shield": ["Gears orbit the target's body and turn aside incoming attacks. For the duration the target gains a +2 bonus to AC and to Dexterity and Constitution saving throws.",
 "Gears orbit the target's body and turn aside incoming attacks. For the duration the target gains a +2 bonus to AC and to Dexterity and Constitution saving throws. The gears do not hinder its movement, its vision or its own attacks."],
"Ghoul King's Cloak": ['You touch a creature and lend it the power of a ghoul king. For the duration the target gains these benefits. Its AC increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.',
 'You touch a creature and lend it the power of a ghoul king. For the duration the target gains these benefits. Its AC increases by 2, to a maximum of 20. When it takes the Attack action to make a melee or ranged weapon attack, it can make one extra attack of the same kind. It is immune to necrotic and radiant damage. It cannot be reduced to less than 1 hit point.'],
"Giant's Jest": ['You enlarge a weapon or other object you can see within range so that it is sized for a Gargantuan creature.',
 'You enlarge a weapon or other object you can see within range so that it is sized for a Gargantuan creature. The object weighs twelve times its normal weight and, in most cases, Huge or smaller creatures cannot use it effectively. It keeps all its usual qualities, including magical powers and effects. It returns to normal size when the spell ends.'],
"Gift of Azathoth": ['A willing creature you touch is filled with the stubborn endurance of pure Chaos. Until the spell ends, the target has advantage on its first three death saving throws.',
 'A willing creature you touch is filled with the stubborn endurance of pure Chaos. Until the spell ends, the target has advantage on its first three death saving throws.'],
"Gift of Luck": ['You give a creature you touch a limited gift of luck. While the spell lasts, the target can choose to have advantage on any three rolls. The spell ends once three rolls have been affected.',
 'You give a creature you touch a limited gift of luck. While the spell lasts, the target can choose to have advantage on any three rolls. The spell ends once three rolls have been affected.'],
"Gift of Resilience": ["A willing creature you touch has advantage on the first three death saving throws it makes before the spell's duration runs out.",
 "A willing creature you touch has advantage on the first three death saving throws it makes before the spell's duration runs out."],
"Gird the Spirit": ['Your magic shields the target from the life-draining energy of Undead.',
 "Your magic shields the target from the life-draining energy of Undead. For the duration the target is immune to effects from Undead that reduce its ability scores, such as a shadow's Strength Drain, or its hit point maximum, such as a specter's Life Drain. The spell does not stop the damage from those attacks. It stops only the reduction to ability scores or hit point maximum."],
"Glacial Cascade": ['You release pure cold in a 30-foot-radius sphere. Each creature in the sphere other than you makes a Constitution save and takes 10d8 cold damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.',
 'You release pure cold in a 30-foot-radius sphere. Each creature in the sphere other than you makes a Constitution save and takes 10d8 cold damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A creature killed by this spell turns to ice and leaves no trace of its original body.'],
"Glacial Fog": ['A frigid fog fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within range. Each creature in the area at the start of its turn while the spell lasts makes a Constitution save.',
 'A frigid fog fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within range. Each creature in the area at the start of its turn while the spell lasts makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 12d6 cold damage, gains one level of exhaustion, and has disadvantage on Perception checks until the start of its next turn. On a success it takes half the damage and ignores the other effects. The fog also freezes stored gear. Crossbow mechanisms turn sluggish, weapons stick in scabbards, potions freeze and bag cords freeze shut. Such items need heat applied for 1 round or longer before they work again.'],
"Glamer of Mundanity": ['You lay a glamer on a creature you touch that makes it easy to overlook and forget.',
 'You lay a glamer on a creature you touch that makes it easy to overlook and forget. For the duration, Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice the target, and ability checks to recall details about it or interactions with it, are made with disadvantage. The target has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks but disadvantage on Charisma checks while the glamer lasts.'],
"Gliding Step": ['As long as you carry no more than your carrying capacity, you walk across the surface of snow instead of wading through it, and snow does not slow your movement.',
 'As long as you carry no more than your carrying capacity, you walk across the surface of snow instead of wading through it, and snow does not slow your movement. Ice holds your weight however thin it is, and you move on ice as if you wore ice skates. You still leave tracks as normal.'],
"Glimpse of the Void": ['You mutter in Void Speech and force images of terror and nonexistence on your foes. Each creature in a 30-foot cube centered on a point within range makes an Intelligence save.',
 'You mutter in Void Speech and force images of terror and nonexistence on your foes. Each creature in a 30-foot cube centered on a point within range makes an Intelligence save. On a fail the creature goes insane for the duration. While insane it takes no actions except to shriek, wail, gibber and babble. The GM controls its erratic movement.'],
"Glimpse the End": ['You study the life force of a creature you touch and sense when it will end.',
 'You study the life force of a creature you touch and sense when it will end. You and the creature share a vision of the most likely way it will die, and you both sense roughly how far in the future that moment lies. The vision is not a prophecy or a fixed fate. It is only the likeliest outcome now, and it changes if the creature changes the course of its life. The vision can feel as short as a few moments or as long as 30 minutes, but in the world around you the knowledge arrives instantly.'],
"Gloomwrought Barrier": ['You raise a barrier of energy drawn from the realm of death and shadow. It is a wall 20 feet high and 60 feet long, or a ring 20 feet high and 20 feet across.',
 'You raise a barrier of energy drawn from the realm of death and shadow. It is a wall 20 feet high and 60 feet long, or a ring 20 feet high and 20 feet across. From one side, which you choose, the wall is transparent. From the other side it is translucent and lightly obscures the area beyond. A creature that tries to move through the wall makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it stops in front of the wall and is frightened until the start of its next turn, when it can try again. A creature that succeeds on the save is immune to the barrier from then on.'],
"Gluey Globule": ['You make a ranged spell attack to hurl a glob of sticky magical glue at a creature within 120 feet. On a hit, the target is restrained.',
 "You make a ranged spell attack to hurl a glob of sticky magical glue at a creature within 120 feet. On a hit, the target is restrained. A restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength save and break free, and it takes 2d6 slashing damage as the glue tears its skin. If your attack roll was a critical hit or beat the target's AC by 5 or more, the Strength save is made with disadvantage. The target is also freed by universal solvent or by taking 20 acid damage. The glue dissolves when the creature breaks free or after 1 minute. You can instead glue an object to a solid surface or to another object. In that case the spell works like one application of sovereign glue and lasts for 1 hour."],
"Glyph of Shifting": ["You trace a hidden glyph on a surface or object you touch. You may also choose a location you know, within 5 miles and on the same plane, as the glyph's destination.",
 "You trace a hidden glyph on a surface or object you touch. You may also choose a location you know, within 5 miles and on the same plane, as the glyph's destination. The glyph triggers when a creature unaware of it touches it. The creature makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it is teleported to the destination. If you set no destination, it takes 4d4 force damage and is knocked prone instead. The glyph vanishes after it triggers or when the duration ends."],
"Goat's Hoof Charm": ['A creature you touch climbs rough slopes with the sure feet of a mountain goat. When it climbs a slope that would normally be difficult terrain for it, it can move at full speed.',
 'A creature you touch climbs rough slopes with the sure feet of a mountain goat. When it climbs a slope that would normally be difficult terrain for it, it can move at full speed. The target also gets a +2 bonus on Dexterity checks and saves made to avoid falling, to catch a ledge or otherwise stop a fall, and to move along a narrow ledge.'],
"Going in Circles": ['You make natural terrain in a 1-mile cube hard to cross.',
 'You make natural terrain in a 1-mile cube hard to cross. A creature in the area has disadvantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to follow tracks or travel safely through it, because the paths seem to twist and turn without sense. The terrain does not change, only the perception of those inside. A creature that succeeds on two Wisdom (Survival) checks in the area sees through the illusion and sees the false twists laid over the real land. A creature that leaves and re-enters the area before the spell ends is affected again even if it succeeded before. A creature with truesight sees through the illusion and is unaffected. A creature that casts find the path automatically finds a way out. When you cast the spell you can set a password. A creature that speaks it while entering the area sees the illusion at once and is unaffected. If you cast this spell on the same spot every day for one year, the illusion lasts until dispelled.'],
"Gordolay's Pleasant Aroma": ['You create an intoxicating scent that fills the area within 30 feet of a point you can see within range. Creatures there find it so pleasing that it distracts them.',
 "You create an intoxicating scent that fills the area within 30 feet of a point you can see within range. Creatures there find it so pleasing that it distracts them. Each creature in the area that makes an attack roll must first make a Wisdom save. On a fail, the attack is made with disadvantage. Only a creature's first attack each round is affected, and later attacks resolve normally. On a success, the creature becomes immune to this scent, though a new casting of the spell can affect it again."],
"Grain of Truth": ['You gain a flash of supernatural insight or advice.',
 "You gain a flash of supernatural insight or advice. The first Intelligence or Charisma ability check you make within 1 minute is made with advantage, and you can add double your proficiency bonus to it. At the GM's discretion, the spell can instead give you general advice equal to the benefit of an augury spell."],
"Grasp of the Tupilak": ['This spell works only against an arcane or divine spellcaster that prepares spells in advance and has at least one unexpended spell slot of 6th level or lower.',
 "This spell works only against an arcane or divine spellcaster that prepares spells in advance and has at least one unexpended spell slot of 6th level or lower. If you hit such a creature with a melee attack before the spell ends, the target also takes 2d4 necrotic damage and some of its available spell slots pass to you for your own use. Roll a d6. The result is the total levels of the slots transferred. Slots of the highest possible level move first, then lower ones. For example, with a roll of 5 and a 5th-level slot available, that slot moves to you. If the target's highest available slot is 3rd level, you might get a 3rd-level and a 2nd-level slot, or a 3rd-level and two 1st-level slots if it has no 2nd-level slot. If the target has no available slot of a suitable level, such as when you roll a 2 and it has used all its 1st and 2nd-level slots, the spell has no effect and deals no necrotic damage. A stolen slot higher than any level you can use counts as the highest level you can use. Unused stolen slots return to where they came from when you take a long rest or when the creature you took them from benefits from remove curse, greater restoration or similar magic."],
"Grave Sense": ['You touch a willing Undead creature or one under your control. For the duration, you can use an action to see through its eyes and hear through its ears until the start of your next turn.',
 'You touch a willing Undead creature or one under your control. For the duration, you can use an action to see through its eyes and hear through its ears until the start of your next turn. This includes its darkvision, blindsight, tremorsense or truesight. You use your own ability scores and skill proficiencies to notice things and interpret what you sense.'],
"Greater Analyze Device": ['You learn every mechanical property, mechanism and function of one construct, clockwork device, mechanical trap or magic item, including how to activate or deactivate those functions where that applies.',
 'You learn every mechanical property, mechanism and function of one construct, clockwork device, mechanical trap or magic item, including how to activate or deactivate those functions where that applies.'],
"Greater Ley Pulse": ['You send ley energy vibrating through a 20-foot cube within range and name one damage type.',
 'You send ley energy vibrating through a 20-foot cube within range and name one damage type. Each creature in the area must succeed on a Wisdom save or lose its immunity to that damage type for the duration.'],
"Greater Maze": ['This spell works like maze, except the target makes a Dexterity save each time it starts its turn in the maze. On a fail it takes 4d6 psychic damage, or half as much on a success.',
 'This spell works like maze, except the target makes a Dexterity save each time it starts its turn in the maze. On a fail it takes 4d6 psychic damage, or half as much on a success. Escape is harder too. The target must use an action to make a DC 20 Intelligence check and escapes when it succeeds on a second check.'],
"Greater Protective Nimbus": ['You wrap yourself in a powerful corona that sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for another 30 feet. Until the spell ends, you have resistance to necrotic and radiant damage.',
 'You wrap yourself in a powerful corona that sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for another 30 feet. Until the spell ends, you have resistance to necrotic and radiant damage. You can use an action to end the spell early, which releases a blast of light in a 30-foot radius. The blast deals 4d8 radiant damage to each creature in the area, and you heal the same amount of damage.'],
"Greater Seal of Sanctuary": ['You inscribe an angelic seal on the ground, floor or other solid surface of a structure. It creates a spherical sanctuary with a 100-foot radius centered on the seal.',
 'You inscribe an angelic seal on the ground, floor or other solid surface of a structure. It creates a spherical sanctuary with a 100-foot radius centered on the seal. Aberrations, elementals, fey, fiends and Undead that come within 5 feet of the boundary know they are about to touch a deadly barrier. If such a creature touches the boundary or tries to cross it by any means, including teleportation and extradimensional travel, it makes a Charisma save. On a fail it takes 15d8 radiant damage, is pushed to 5 feet outside the boundary, and cannot target anything inside with attacks, spells or abilities until the spell ends. On a success it takes half as much radiant damage and can cross. A fiend that is not on its home plane is destroyed at once instead, with no save. Aberrations, elementals, fey and Undead inside the boundary have disadvantage on ability checks, attack rolls and saving throws, and each takes 4d8 radiant damage at the start of its turn. Other creatures cannot be charmed or frightened while within 100 feet of the seal. The seal has AC 18, 75 hit points, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage, and immunity to psychic and poison damage. Ranged attacks against it have disadvantage. If you scribe it on an object that is later destroyed, such as a wooden door, the seal is not harmed and stays in place, perhaps hanging in midair. The spell ends only if the seal drops to 0 hit points.'],
"Green Decay": ['Your touch spreads a nauseating alien rot. Make a melee spell attack against a creature within reach.',
 "Your touch spreads a nauseating alien rot. Make a melee spell attack against a creature within reach. On a hit, the creature catches the supernatural disease green decay, and creatures within 15 feet of the target that can see it make a Constitution save or become poisoned until the end of their next turn. You lose concentration if you cannot see the target at the end of your turn.\n\n**Green Decay.** A virulent extraterrestrial fungus slowly eats the creature's flesh. While the disease lasts, the creature has disadvantage on Charisma and Wisdom checks and on Wisdom saves, and it is vulnerable to acid, fire and necrotic damage. At the end of each of its turns it makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 1d6 necrotic damage and its hit point maximum drops by the same amount. If it gets three successes before three failures, the disease ends at once, but the damage and the maximum reduction remain. If it gets three failures first, the disease lasts for the spell's duration and no more saves are allowed."],
"Green Mantle": ['You take on the look of the terrain around you. In a forest, grass and tiny mushrooms sprout from your hair, moss grows on your chin, and your skin turns mottled leaf green and bark brown.',
 'You take on the look of the terrain around you. In a forest, grass and tiny mushrooms sprout from your hair, moss grows on your chin, and your skin turns mottled leaf green and bark brown. In an arctic grassland, gray lichen and boreal grasses cloak you. In suitable terrain you get a +2 bonus to Stealth checks.'],
"Gremlins": ['You target a construct and summon a plague of invisible spirits to torment it. The target makes a Wisdom save and negates the spell on a success.',
 'You target a construct and summon a plague of invisible spirits to torment it. The target makes a Wisdom save and negates the spell on a success. While the spell lasts, the construct has disadvantage on attack rolls, ability checks and saving throws, and it takes 3d8 force damage at the start of each of its turns as the spirits take it apart.'],
"Grim Siphon": ['You twist the forces of entropy around two creatures, bringing pain to one and holding off the end of the other. A creature you can see within range makes a Constitution save.',
 'You twist the forces of entropy around two creatures, bringing pain to one and holding off the end of the other. A creature you can see within range makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes poison damage equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting ability modifier. Another creature you choose within 5 feet of the target regains hit points equal to half the poison damage dealt.'],
"Grinding Gears": ['You choose a spot within range and huge gears rise from the ground there, making a 20-foot radius of difficult terrain.',
 'You choose a spot within range and huge gears rise from the ground there, making a 20-foot radius of difficult terrain. A creature moving in the area makes a Dexterity save after every 10 feet of movement and when it stands up. On a fail it falls prone and takes 1d8 bludgeoning damage.'],
"Grudge Match": ['This spell affects creatures you designate within range, but only if the group has equal numbers of allies and enemies. If the numbers differ, the spell fails.',
 'This spell affects creatures you designate within range, but only if the group has equal numbers of allies and enemies. If the numbers differ, the spell fails. For the duration, each target gets a +2 bonus on saving throws, attack rolls, ability checks, skill checks and weapon damage rolls that involve other targets of the spell. All affected creatures can recognize the other targets by sight. If an affected creature makes any of those rolls against a creature that is not a target, it takes a -2 penalty on the roll.'],
"Guest of Honor": ['You can cast this spell only as a ritual. You whisper words of encouragement and a creature you touch gains confidence and the approval of strangers.',
 'You can cast this spell only as a ritual. You whisper words of encouragement and a creature you touch gains confidence and the approval of strangers. For the duration, the target puts its best foot forward and strangers link it with positive feelings. The target adds 1d4 to all Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to sway the attitudes of others.\n\n**Group Spellcasting.** When other spellcasters help you cast this spell, it lasts 10 minutes longer for each spellcaster other than you, up to a maximum of 90 minutes.\n\n**Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, the effect lasts 24 hours.'],
"Guiding Star": ['By watching the stars or the position of the sun, you learn the cardinal directions and the direction and distance to a destination you name.',
 'By watching the stars or the position of the sun, you learn the cardinal directions and the direction and distance to a destination you name. You cannot become disoriented or lose track of that destination. The spell does not show the best route and does not warn you of gorges, flooded rivers or other impassable or dangerous terrain.'],
"Hamstring": ['You shape an arrow of eldritch energy and send it at a target you can see within range. Make a ranged spell attack.',
 'You shape an arrow of eldritch energy and send it at a target you can see within range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 force damage and cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn. The damage increases by 1d4 at 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4) and 17th level (4d4).'],
"Hand of Doom": ['Your outstretched hand glows with sinister power that speeds the end of a creature you touch. Make a melee spell attack against it.',
 'Your outstretched hand glows with sinister power that speeds the end of a creature you touch. Make a melee spell attack against it. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 necrotic damage and makes a Constitution save. On a fail it is poisoned until the end of your next turn. If the target was already poisoned when you hit it, it takes 1d12 poison damage instead of the 1d4 necrotic damage. The damage increases by one die at 5th level (2d4 necrotic or 2d12 poison), 11th level (3d4 or 3d12) and 17th level (4d4 or 4d12).'],
"Hard Heart": ['You imbue your touch with the power to make a creature cold, aloof and unfeeling. The creature you touch while casting makes a Wisdom save, and it can choose to fail unless it is currently charmed.',
 'You imbue your touch with the power to make a creature cold, aloof and unfeeling. The creature you touch while casting makes a Wisdom save, and it can choose to fail unless it is currently charmed. On a success the spell fails. On a fail, the target is immune to being charmed for the duration, and any charm on it ends. Charisma checks made against the target also have disadvantage for the duration.'],
"Harry": ['You fill the target with a sense of insecurity and terror it cannot shake. The target makes a Wisdom save.',
 'You fill the target with a sense of insecurity and terror it cannot shake. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it has disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to avoid your notice and is frightened of you while you are in its line of sight. While you are within 1 mile of the target, you have advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track it, and it cannot take a long rest, afraid that you are just around the corner. The target can repeat the save once every 10 minutes and ends the spell on a success. On a success from the first save, the target is not affected and you cannot use this spell on it again for 24 hours.'],
"Harsh Light of Summer's Glare": ['You release a burst of brilliant light that bears down on every creature within range that can see you. Creatures with darkvision that fail a Constitution save are blinded and stunned.',
 'You release a burst of brilliant light that bears down on every creature within range that can see you. Creatures with darkvision that fail a Constitution save are blinded and stunned. Creatures without darkvision that fail the save are blinded. This is not a gaze attack, so averting the eyes or wearing a blindfold does not prevent it.'],
"Heart to Heart": ['For the duration, you and a creature you touch stay stable and unconscious if one of you drops to 0 hit points while the other has 1 or more.',
 'For the duration, you and a creature you touch stay stable and unconscious if one of you drops to 0 hit points while the other has 1 or more. If you touch a dying creature, it becomes stable but stays unconscious while it has 0 hit points. If both of you drop to 0 hit points, you both make death saving throws as normal. When either of you regains hit points, that person can split them between the two of you if you are within 60 feet of each other.'],
"Heart-Seeking Arrow": ["The next time you make a ranged weapon attack during the duration, the ammunition, or the weapon itself if it is a thrown weapon, flies toward the target's vital organs.",
 "The next time you make a ranged weapon attack during the duration, the ammunition, or the weapon itself if it is a thrown weapon, flies toward the target's vital organs. Make the attack roll as normal. On a hit, the weapon deals an extra 6d6 damage of its usual type. On a miss it still deals half that extra damage as it streaks toward the target. If the attack reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target has disadvantage on its next death saving throw, and if it dies it can be restored to life only by true resurrection or wish. The spell has no effect on Undead or constructs."],
"Heartache": ['You make an enemy feel the pangs of unrequited love and emotional pain, so intense that the target makes a Charisma save and takes 5d6 psychic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.',
 'You make an enemy feel the pangs of unrequited love and emotional pain, so intense that the target makes a Charisma save and takes 5d6 psychic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.'],
"Heartstop": ["You slow a willing target's heartbeat to one beat per minute and its breathing nearly stops. To a casual or brief observer the target looks dead.",
 "You slow a willing target's heartbeat to one beat per minute and its breathing nearly stops. To a casual or brief observer the target looks dead. When the spell ends, the creature returns to normal with no ill effects."],
"Heartstrike": ['The spirits of ancient archers guide your missiles to their marks. Until the start of your next turn, you have advantage on ranged weapon attacks.',
 'The spirits of ancient archers guide your missiles to their marks. Until the start of your next turn, you have advantage on ranged weapon attacks. When making those attacks you ignore penalties for half cover, three-quarters cover and light obscurement.'],
"Heavenly Crown": ['A glowing golden crown appears on your head and sheds dim light in a 30-foot radius.',
 'A glowing golden crown appears on your head and sheds dim light in a 30-foot radius. When you cast the spell, and as a bonus action on later turns until it ends, you can choose one willing creature within 30 feet that you can see. If the target can hear you, it can use its reaction to make one melee weapon attack and then move up to half its speed, or move first and then attack.'],
"Hedren's Birds of Clay": ['You create a number of clay pigeons equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting modifier (minimum of one) that swirl around you.',
 'You create a number of clay pigeons equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting modifier (minimum of one) that swirl around you. When you are the target of a ranged weapon attack or a ranged spell attack, before the attack roll is made, you can use your reaction to shout "Pull!" One clay pigeon then moves to block the attack. If the attack roll is less than 10 + your proficiency bonus, the attack misses. Otherwise make a check using your spellcasting ability modifier and compare it to the attack roll. If your result is higher, the attack is intercepted and has no effect. Whether or not the attack is intercepted, one clay pigeon is used up. The spell ends when the last pigeon is used.'],
"Hellfire Blitz": ['You take on a flaming spectral form until the end of your turn and at once move up to 40 feet in a straight line.',
 'You take on a flaming spectral form until the end of your turn and at once move up to 40 feet in a straight line. You can pass through spaces occupied by other creatures but must end your turn in an unoccupied space. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks. Each creature whose space you pass through makes a Dexterity save and takes 6d6 fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. You leave a line of hellfire 5 feet wide along your path. It burns for a number of rounds equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. A creature that ends its turn in the hellfire or passes through the line on its turn makes a Dexterity save and takes 1d6 fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A creature takes this damage only once per turn.'],
"Hellforging": ['You spend an hour calling forth a disembodied evil spirit. At the end of that time, the spirit makes a Charisma save.',
 'You spend an hour calling forth a disembodied evil spirit. At the end of that time, the spirit makes a Charisma save. If it succeeds, you take 2d10 psychic damage plus 2d10 necrotic damage from waves of wild energy rippling out from the spirit. You can maintain the spell, forcing the spirit to repeat the save at the end of each of your turns, with the same cost to you for each success. If you choose not to maintain it or cannot, the spirit returns to its place of torment and cannot be recalled. If the save fails, the spirit moves into the waiting soul gem and at once animates the constructed body. The subject is now a hellforged. It loses its previous racial traits and gains gearforged traits, with these changes.\n\n**Vulnerability.** Hellforged are vulnerable to radiant damage.\n\n**Evil Mind.** Hellforged have disadvantage on saves against spells and abilities of evil fiends or aberrations that affect the mind or behavior.\n\n**Past Life.** The hellforged keeps only a vague sense of who it was before, but enough to gain proficiency in one skill.\n\n**Languages.** Hellforged speak Common, Machine Speech, and Infernal or Abyssal.\n\nUp to four other spellcasters of at least 5th level can help with the ritual. Each helper raises the DC of the Charisma save by 1. If the save succeeds, you and each helper take the damage. A helper who drops out of the casting cannot rejoin.'],
"Hematomancy": ['You can learn about a creature whose blood you hold. The target makes a Wisdom save. If it knows you are casting the spell, it can choose to fail.',
 "You can learn about a creature whose blood you hold. The target makes a Wisdom save. If it knows you are casting the spell, it can choose to fail. On a success, nothing happens and you cannot use this spell on it again for 24 hours. On a fail, or if the blood came from a dead creature, you learn the following.\n- The target's most common name, if any.\n- The target's creature type and subtype if any, its gender, and which of its ability scores is highest (but not the exact score).\n- The target's current status, such as alive, dead, sick, wounded or healthy.\n- How the blood was shed, such as a bleeding wound or a spatter from an attack, and how long ago.\n\n**Beacon.** Instead of learning all of the above, you can use the blood as a beacon. For 1 hour, as long as you are on the same plane as the creature, you know the direction and distance to where the target was when you cast the spell. While you travel toward that location, whenever you face a choice of paths, the spell shows which one is the shortest and most direct."],
"Hero's Steel": ['You fill the metal of a melee weapon you touch with the fearsome aura of a mighty hero. The wielder has advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks made while menacingly brandishing the weapon.',
 'You fill the metal of a melee weapon you touch with the fearsome aura of a mighty hero. The wielder has advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks made while menacingly brandishing the weapon. An opponent with 30 or fewer hit points that is struck by the weapon makes a Charisma save or is stunned for 1 round. If the creature has more than 30 hit points but fewer than the wielder currently has, it is frightened instead. A frightened creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on a success. A creature that succeeds on the save is immune to castings of this spell on the same weapon for 24 hours.'],
"Hide in One's Shadow": ["You touch a willing creature with a piece of charcoal while casting. The target and everything it carries blend into the target's shadow, which stays visible while the body seems to vanish.",
 "You touch a willing creature with a piece of charcoal while casting. The target and everything it carries blend into the target's shadow, which stays visible while the body seems to vanish. The shadow is incorporeal, weightless, and immune to all damage except psychic and radiant. The target stays aware of its surroundings and can move, but only as a shadow could, flowing along surfaces as if moving normally. The creature can step out of the shadow at will, taking its physical form in the shadow's space and ending the spell. You cannot cast this spell in an area with no light at all, where no shadow would form. Even faint light such as moonlight or starlight is enough. If the light source is removed, or the shadow is flooded with light so that the creature would cast no shadow, the spell ends and the creature reappears in the shadow's space."],
"Hoarfrost": ['A melee weapon you are holding is infused with cold. For the duration, frost coats the weapon and light vapor rises from it if the air is above freezing.',
 'A melee weapon you are holding is infused with cold. For the duration, frost coats the weapon and light vapor rises from it if the air is above freezing. The weapon becomes magical and deals an extra 1d4 cold damage on a hit. The spell ends after 1 minute, or earlier if you hit with the weapon or let go of it. The damage increases by 1d4 at 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4) and 17th level (4d4).'],
"Hobble": ['You create an ethereal trap in the space of a creature you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity save or its speed is halved until the end of its next turn.',
 'You create an ethereal trap in the space of a creature you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity save or its speed is halved until the end of its next turn.'],
"Hobble Mount": ['Make a melee spell attack against a horse, wolf or other four-legged or two-legged beast that is being ridden as a mount.',
 'Make a melee spell attack against a horse, wolf or other four-legged or two-legged beast that is being ridden as a mount. On a hit, the beast is disabled and cannot move at its normal speed without injury. An affected creature that moves more than half its base speed in a turn takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage. The spell has no effect on a creature your GM does not consider a mount.'],
"Holy Ground": ['You call on divine power to bless the ground within 60 feet of you.',
 'You call on divine power to bless the ground within 60 feet of you. Creatures slain in the area cannot be raised as Undead by magic or by monster abilities, even if the corpse is later moved out of the area. Any spell of 4th level or lower that would summon or animate Undead in the area fails automatically. Such spells cast with a slot of 5th level or higher work normally.'],
"Holy Vow": ['You willingly take a vow to finish a task or carry out a service. The task cannot conflict with your alignment or your sacred oath.',
 "You willingly take a vow to finish a task or carry out a service. The task cannot conflict with your alignment or your sacred oath. While you serve under the vow, for as long as the spell lasts, your hit point maximum and current hit points increase by 10. Whenever you make an attack roll or a saving throw, roll a d4 and add the result. These benefits apply only to activities that directly relate to your task, or to situations that get in the way of carrying it out, such as random encounters on the road. If you willingly give up your vow, the spell ends and you take 4d10 psychic damage. At the GM's discretion you may suffer other penalties and need to atone. Failing to complete the task brings no penalty as long as you stay true to the vow. You are also not penalized if outside coercion, magical or otherwise, makes you give it up, such as being charmed or a villain threatening innocents if you do not break the vow."],
"Holy Warding": ['You make a protective gesture toward your allies. Choose three creatures you can see within range.',
 'You make a protective gesture toward your allies. Choose three creatures you can see within range. Until the end of your next turn, the chosen allies have resistance to nonmagical weapon attacks, including bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. If a target moves farther than 30 feet from you, the effect ends for that creature.'],
"Hone Blade": ['You magically sharpen the edge of a bladed weapon or object. The target weapon gets +1 to damage on its next successful hit.',
 'You magically sharpen the edge of a bladed weapon or object. The target weapon gets +1 to damage on its next successful hit.'],
"Hunger of Leng": ['You curse a creature you can see within range with an insatiable ghoulish appetite. If it has a digestive system, it makes a Wisdom save.',
 'You curse a creature you can see within range with an insatiable ghoulish appetite. If it has a digestive system, it makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it is compelled to eat the flesh of living creatures for the duration. On its turn the target gains a bite attack and moves to attack the closest creature that is not Undead or a construct. The target is proficient with the bite and adds its Strength modifier to the attack and damage rolls. The bite deals piercing damage with a d4 damage die. If the target is larger than Medium, the die increases by 1d4 for each size category above Medium. The target also has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that does not have all its hit points. If no valid creature is within reach, the target instead deals piercing damage to itself equal to 2d4 + its Strength modifier. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on a success. If it fails twice in a row, the spell lasts its full duration with no more saves.'],
}
